The $\%$ symbol means percent, which is per hundred.

$\begin{align}
50\text{ per }100&=\dfrac{50}{100}\\\\
&=\dfrac{1}{2} \cdot \dfrac{50}{50}\\\\
&=\dfrac{1}{2}
\end{align}$

The $\%$ symbol means percent, which is per hundred.

$\begin{align}
250\text{ per }100&=\dfrac{250}{100}\\\\
&=\dfrac{5}{2} \cdot \dfrac{50}{50}\\\\
&=\dfrac{5}{2}
\end{align}$
